WEBVTT

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.330
The story until now.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:13.800
With a single word by Leah Dizon, the Nishiogi-Kubo International Film Festival was opened.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.870
To the folks who insisted it was a "paradise of cinema",

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:21.780
those who planned to revitalize a village with anime were not interesting at all.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:27.450
With grudging, forced consent, taking a megaphone and caught in a veritable honey trap,

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:32.890
they became enveloped in a rampant love like that felt by a modern girlie-girl maiden in Uno Chiyo.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:38.950
As a result, on the false pretense that the first kanji in the word "delusion" is insulting to women,

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:45.850
they were told "<i>Love Confessions</i>, <i>Love Confessions</i>!" in Fujin bleep-ron,

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:49.330
the shameful love confession of having their nipples covered in syrup and then being buried in an anthill.

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:58.670
At that moment, with the single word "Cut!", Mizuno Haruo, dressed as an American policeman, appeared.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:49.980
Oora! It's already next week!

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:50.150
Exhibition sales

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:50.320
Eurian

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:50.480
Deposit sales

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:50.650
Futures sales

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:50.820
Furniture lease sales

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:51.080
Date sales

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:57.250
She's been there since the week before last.

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:59.260
Such a placid girl.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.980
I've been treated so horribly these past two weeks.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:04.000
Teacher.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:10.690
Hey.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.070
Oh, teacher!

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.920
How about one?

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.710
Ice for ¥10,000?

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:22.910
There's no way it'll sell at that price.

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:24.730
You won't buy any?

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:25.720
Not at all.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:29.590
Hey.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:31.090
Oh, teacher!

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:32.540
How about some?

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:39.190
What a bargain!

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.630
I'll buy, I'll buy!

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:43.600
Thanks!

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.990
This was a good deal.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.610
Suddenly, fierce solar rays!?

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:53.950
It's going bad before my eyes!

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:56.580
No matter where I dodge to, the solar rays follow me!

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.190
I'll have to buy ice at a nearby convenience store!

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:02.840
The closest one is a ten-minute walk.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:06.820
Oh no, my maguro's gonna rot! What do I do!?{el - taihen da}

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:07.800
Teacher.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:12.940
Sold!

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.270
Thanks!

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.440
All right! That's a load off my back!

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.130
Thanks a lot!

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:25.620
{fuck I keep wanting to abbreviate him as "Bo" for "Bondster".} Like that, huh?

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.180
Perfect.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.810
You're great. Well done.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:35.450
Oh man!

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:38.140
Why did you waste money like this!?

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:40.060
It's strange, isn't it.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:42.910
Sure, the maguro was a pretty good find,

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:45.760
but you can't spend ten thousand yen on a block of ice!

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:50.800
That's what's called a loss leader.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.400
It's a common business model.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:54.780
You were there?

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:56.640
Always.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.540
For example, printers.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:01.380
The units themselves are really cheap now.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:04.780
But in exchange, the ink's expensive.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.090
So they make their profit off the ink?

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.990
That's right. There are other examples, too.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:13.230
After growing your thousand free hairs, you can't go back

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.960
and will spend incredible amounts of money!

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:18.050
Copiers and stuff are bought incredibly cheap,

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.760
and the profit is made on the maintenance!

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:22.200
There really are a lot of things like that.

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:27.630
When you buy into a timeshare as a matter of course {->because the price is so low it's nothing to even consider}

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:28.230
That's cheap!

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:28.910
We'll take it!

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:32.840
but the maintenance fees are ¥100,000 a month and you have to take out a loan, is the same! {selfedit this line later}{kaedit (if I may suggest...): It's like buying into a ultra-cheap timeshare without a second thought, only to wind up needing a loan for the ¥100,000 monthly maintenance.}

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:36.430
Dr. **rton is free for three months,

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:41.220
but then he warns you constantly of the dangers you would face witout him, and you buy it!

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:47.890
I'm in despair!

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:51.260
Businesses which make up the money later have left me in despair!

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.670
The two of you...

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:09.230
Wasting your allowance again, Majiru?

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:13.350
It's not a waste! This thing's great!

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.280
Every issue comes with parts!

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:18.090
Put them all together, and it makes a combining robot!

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:21.360
And every issue is only ¥190!

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.460
Isn't it a value!

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:25.670
Starting next issue, it's ¥500.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.920
That really is the same marketing.

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:32.470
I was caught by it, too.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:34.620
“Weekly Travel Pack”.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:38.480
Buy every issue, and at the end, you'll go on a journey.

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:43.350
Volume 1 was “bath beads A”, volume 2 was “bath beads B”.

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:45.670
Being able to go on a journey in only two weeks...

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.350
Well, it is pretty honest.

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:49.850
I see.

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:54.090
Now that I think of it, Teacher is pretty popular with the girls.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:02.270
This is—

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:07.610
Haven't your portions been a bit small lately?

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:10.240
It's because you've wasted your money, Majiru.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.620
I haven't wasted that much.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:15.910
If you don't like it, I won't make anything for you.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:20.050
She's been acting funny lately.

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:23.250
I wonder if she's not wasting her money on something.

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:25.560
This is—!

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:31.160
"Every month comes with human body parts! Put them together, and in the end, you'll have Zetsubou-sensei!”?

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:56.130
Oh no! Kiri's gonna kill me!

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:58.260
What's up, Majiru?

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:20.910
Just what is this...

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:22.490
What's the meaning of this?

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:27.920
Unfortunately, Itoshiki Nozomu, you have already died once in a mysterious explosion.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:28.920
See?

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:35.160
The contents of your brain have been programmed into an AI,

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:40.430
and the scientific talents of shut-ins across the land have come together to revive you as an android!

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:42.990
Don't you know the Three Laws of Robotics?

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:45.400
You must absolutely obey the orders of your creator! {sign wording}

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.410
All right, this is the final part.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:49.810
The tabi? {kaedit: what is "tabi" supposed to be?}

00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:51.410
Oh no, I've gotta hide!

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:53.140
All right.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:58.220
“Just after completion, it will act as the creator wills...”, huh?{kaedit (old-school scifi geek): equivalent truncation of direct Asimov quote = "A robot must obey any orders given to it by humans..."}

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:12.160
Kiss me.

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:18.320
No way! I'm such a fool!

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:20.470
What am I making my creation do!?

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:23.810
I take that back. Go clean the gutters.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:33.880
And this is...?

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:36.990
I told you, I got tired of it after the first issue!

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:46.560
It's chilly.

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:50.100
... Nope, not really.

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:53.770
This winter has been really mild.

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:58.840
There's someone passed out!

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:01.080
He's—!

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.820
General Frost!

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:03.990
What, outta money after moving to a new office!?

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:04.150
Gotta cut corners to make a profit, huh!?

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:04.320
Your production costs are the same but other companies are selling a lot better!

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:04.490
You really can't pull this off at the same time as Ghostory, can you!

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:04.650
The pictures aren't moving!  You can't even call this animation!

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:04.920
The anime industry's collapsing!

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:11.520
General Frost!

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:15.590
He's General Frost!

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.890
He's so weak!

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.840
General Frost is a person!?

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:24.170
I thought it was the Siberian cold air mass!

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:29.910
With General Frost this weak, winters will be mild.

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:32.810
Don't be so solemn while lying!

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:36.650
He's a person of high status, so let's hospitably bring him to the classroom.

00:10:42.020 --> 00:10:44.520
How fare thee, milord?

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:48.160
Been better.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:53.730
If General Frost ends up like that, ski areas and the leggings industry will be inconvenienced.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:56.480
Honestly...

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:59.270
I've been thinking of quitting as General Frost.

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:05.010
What are you saying!? Were you to quit, Hirose Komi would be crestfallen!

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:11.850
But with this winter so mild, you can't really call him General Frost, can you?

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:15.590
More like Colonel Frost.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:20.530
Colonel? <i>Colonel!?</i>

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.460
What are you saying, Kitsu!?

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:25.460
To soldiers, rank is more important than their lives!

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:28.960
Your rank will follow it down.

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:30.800
To be honest, that's it.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:34.470
I want to stop being General Frost, but not stop being a general.

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:36.350
That's right.

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:40.480
Once you've experienced being a general, you can't be anything else.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:45.480
All right, let's go to Hello Work and see if they're hiring generals!

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.090
Anywhere hiring generals?

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:52.350
There ain't nothing.

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:56.590
I'm okay with being a General Rowdy or a demon general, instead.

00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:01.910
There's no way you can go from being General Frost to a demon general.

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.740
Yeah, I guess.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:06.970
Crab General is looking for potential managers.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:11.790
Ah, here's one! A pro baseball team general!

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:12.980
Baseball?

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:22.390
We need a pitcher, not a belly-itcher!

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:24.100
A heckling general!?

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:26.990
Hey, the outfielders are gonna catch a cold!

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:32.200
With that kind of heckling, I can't call you a heckling general at all.

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:34.700
More like heckling colonel.

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:35.700
Again!?

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:38.800
Colonel...Colonel again...

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.850
You're stirring things up again! {*}{kaedit (something like): You're stirring shit up again!}

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:42.610
But like that,

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:45.290
he isn't even fit to lick the boots of the legendary Hecklers General! {kaedit: crossed idioms: "wash the feet of" OR "lick the boots of"...same meaning, essentially, but the second is clearly a better fit here.}

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:47.730
Don't you even know the basics of baseball!? {kaedit: more like: Learn some fundamentals!}

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:49.540
I did it a few times with the party leader! {ftw?}

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:51.960
Your sister's an xxx!

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:54.090
Don't just send me weaklings!

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:57.720
Then what kind of heckling is general-class?

00:12:57.720 --> 00:13:00.090
Well, for example...

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:03.860
That's cruel!

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:10.200
Telling Hichori he'll “never win any smiles alone” is too much!

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:12.750
Hold it!

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:21.510
You're so troublesome!

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:23.820
How!?

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:25.520
To draw properly?

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:30.390
I knew it, I can't handle being a heckling general.

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:35.040
We can get away with it nowadays, so why not just tack “General” onto anything?

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.260
For example...

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:38.000
Love General!

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:42.380
Love...General.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:46.170
Love General. That's nice.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:48.510
Love General is pretty good!

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:53.070
I've decided! I'll become a Love General!

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:54.680
What's this “Love General” thing, anyway!?

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:59.190
But if you become a Love General, you've got to have general-class loves.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:01.190
Loves worthy of a general?

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:06.560
Somehow, that's a horrible image.

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:08.290
I quit being a Love General.

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:11.170
Then how about being a Dream General?

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:12.300
Dream General?

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:15.340
I can do that!

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:17.850
I have dreams worthy of a general!

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:19.620
A private car

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:20.920
A private home (with garden)

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.910
Hitting the lotto for ¥60,000,000

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:24.470
Those are the dreams of commoners!

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:25.410
The archetypal ones!

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:27.560
You're not cut out to be a Dream General.

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:29.150
I see.

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:33.690
Lately, the word “Dream” has had a lot of trouble associated with it, so you should probably quit.

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:35.690
Okay, I'll do that.

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:38.990
Other generals, huh. Oh, that's right.

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:40.990
Comics General.

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:43.260
General Metabolic

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:45.000
Miss General

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.430
General Shi-bleep Kosaku

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:49.440
How about these?

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:51.100
What kind of general is <i>that</i>!?

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:54.970
If we're just making up names, I'd like to try being a general too.

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:56.470
Really?

00:14:57.980 --> 00:14:59.290
Comics General.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:01.920
Don't call me a Comics General!

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:05.420
That isn't praise at all, is it!? You're not praising me at all, are you!?

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:08.420
Now, everyone is calling themselves a general!

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:31.730
Why does ‘Normal General’ seem like the best one?

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:33.570
Because it's normal?

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:35.830
Don't call me normal!

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:45.290
Let's give everyone the prestige of being called General!

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:46.790
That just isn't the same, is it!?

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:48.700
Middle-part

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:51.700
I've got to make a part straight down the middle worth of a general.

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:07.480
Is she trying to split the earth in two!?

00:16:07.760 --> 00:16:09.680
Someone please stop her!

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:13.490
There's no one higher-ranking than a general enough to voice their opinion.

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:16.220
There's one person.

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:18.690
Who!?

00:16:18.690 --> 00:16:21.210
Who can give orders to a general!?

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:25.200
Emperor Penguin.

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:28.520
As you will.

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:32.310
Because it's an emperor penguin!?

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:36.890
Which is more eminent, an emperor or a general?

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.050
An emperor is far more eminent.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:42.230
You did great.

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:47.310
Someday, I hope to be Emperor Frost.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.890
This's long!

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:14.970
Happy birthday!

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:17.550
Happy birthday, teacher!

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:24.930
Were you surprised?

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:27.430
It's a surprise party.

00:17:27.430 --> 00:17:27.600
Shocked that there were still no storyboards on editing day

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:27.770
Shocked that the art wasn't done by ADR day

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:27.940
Shocked that dubbing got pushed back a week

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:28.100
Shocked that some cuts weren't done on delivery day

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:28.270
Shocked that we finished the video on broadcast day

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:28.570
Shocked that it actually broadcast at the normal time

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:36.940
That's definitely a surprise!

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:40.510
After all, today isn't my birthday.

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:43.040
Right, it's in November, isn't it?

00:17:44.050 --> 00:17:46.130
So why do it today!?

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:48.480
Didn't you tell us, teacher?

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:55.790
I thought I'd have a surprise birthday party for a friend later.

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:58.460
Surprise?

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:04.920
So...

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.500
It seems like something I'd say, and I feel like I've said it.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:13.910
I want to be with a guy, and always have my heart going pitter-patter.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:19.130
And from time to time, I'd like surprises.

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:22.750
Girls are like that. {resisting urge to ->complicated}

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:23.720
Annoying!

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:26.720
Whose internal monologue was that!?

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:28.950
No one thinks that!

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:30.950
I don't think you're annoying.

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:33.330
I don't think so. I don't think you're boring at all.

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:35.200
All of them!?

00:18:35.200 --> 00:18:39.300
Well, nowadays, even if you don't go looking for them there are plenty of day-to-day surprises in this world.

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:42.940
The surprise of throwing out a PM between elections twice in a row!

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:49.440
The surprise of finding out right before that this time your deadline's a day early!

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:53.330
Finding out that after ten years that your rice was blended with contaminated rice!

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:54.550
That's surp<i>rice</i>! {hurrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrr}{kaedit: if it were me, i'd italicize the -"rice' part. Just adds to the groan-factor.}

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:58.100
The shock of getting together and finding out that everyone at the party decided to bring a horn! {as decoration/party item thing the word's slipping my mind} {kazoo???}

00:18:58.100 --> 00:18:59.820
That's a real surprise party!

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:02.690
Those last two are putting a bit too much of a spin on it.

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:05.090
There are so many no-good surprises!

00:19:05.090 --> 00:19:08.430
Japanese can't be shocked by small things anymore!

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:09.660
That's too bad.

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:14.590
We weren't able to give teacher a surprise party just by changing the date.

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.820
Well, it's the thought that counts.

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:19.920
But it's a bit different from a surprise.

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:25.070
Chiri, I was right, it wasn't a surprise.

00:19:25.070 --> 00:19:26.010
Hold it...

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:27.840
Didn't I tell you?

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:31.610
The real surprise party starts now.

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:39.060
No, I've had enough surprises for now!

00:19:57.740 --> 00:19:59.720
What <i>is</i> this!?

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:02.670
Let's start the surprise party.

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:08.460
And shock teacher with things like a Communist bazaar and a raw meat tasting!

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:13.190
You were all surprised, right?

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:16.430
Well...

00:20:16.430 --> 00:20:19.010
It wasn't a surprise at all.

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:21.780
No, I was plenty surprised!

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:24.800
I thought of several other ways to appear, too.

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:26.300
Appearing from inside!

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:27.710
Appearing in the sky!

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:29.350
Appearing out of someone's pocket!

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:34.420
Well, it's you, Chiri, so no matter what you do, I'm not really surprised.

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:39.830
It's the other way around. If you didn't do anything, just held a normal birthday party, I'd be surprised.

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:41.290
That'd be surprising.

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:42.670
What do you mean!?

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:49.910
It may be more common in modern Japan to be surprised if something isn't done.

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:55.640
Marui, I want to talk with you about something, so can we meet up after class?

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:01.680
What do I do!? My heart isn't ready!

00:22:41.410 --> 00:22:44.550
The Zetsubou-sensei Drawing Song is about to start.

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:46.920
Matching the song, let's draw together, okay?

00:22:48.480 --> 00:22:54.800
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:22:54.800 --> 00:23:01.270
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:02.850
Lightning...

00:23:02.850 --> 00:23:04.510
Flash!

00:23:04.510 --> 00:23:05.990
Lightning...

00:23:05.990 --> 00:23:07.720
Flash!

00:23:07.720 --> 00:23:10.920
The rain comes pouring down.

00:23:10.920 --> 00:23:14.180
From the gaps came the leaks.

00:23:14.180 --> 00:23:16.940
Two puddles were made.

00:23:17.230 --> 00:23:20.500
Let's go fishing, there's the fish hook!

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:24.920
With the fish we caught, we made a fish cake.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:28.440
It's Zetsubou-sensei!

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:31.440
Did everyone draw well?

00:23:31.440 --> 00:23:33.460
Bye bye!
